# CAPA — Menu Setting rollout safety net

Incident (2026-06-04): admin Ankit saw an empty sidebar; auditor Shekhar hit
the page ErrorBoundary. Suspected cause: `menu_overrides_enabled=true` plus
items re-parented under brand-new custom L3 containers (`custom-dashboards`,
`custom-shortcut-*`) hollowed out static groups, and a custom node with
`roles:['admin']` made the resolver path unreliable for non-admins.

## What this CAPA changes (UI/menu/route compatibility ONLY)
- `applyOverrides`: dangling `parent_key` (override OR default) is coerced to
  the default / `null`; `menu_level` is clamped to 1..4. Bad rows can no
  longer break tree traversal.
- `AppSidebar.resolveGroupItems`: wrapped in try/catch (fall back to static
  defaults on any throw); if the resolver yields **zero items** for a group
  whose static fallback was non-empty, return the fallback with resolved
  labels — the baseline never disappears. `synthFromNode` now defaults custom
  items to `ALL_APP_ROLES`; DB `menu_access_config` remains the visibility
  gate.
- `SidebarContent` is wrapped in an `ErrorBoundary` so a single bad node
  cannot blank the entire sidebar.
- **No DB, RLS, workflow, scoring, or audit changes.** Roadmap design intact.

## Baseline access invariants (must hold every release)
- Authenticated users: Dashboard, Inbox, PMS Policy (when policy allows).
- Admin: Admin Dashboard, User Management, System Settings, core admin pages, Reports.
- Auditor: Audit Panel, Explore Employees (Read-Only), Org KPI Audit Review, reports.
- Manager / Management / HR PMS: previous sidebar + route access unchanged.
- `menu_overrides_enabled=true` MUST NOT break any of the above.

## Removal criteria (all must be met before deleting this layer)
1. Production-like fixture with current `menu_registry` + `menu_overrides`
   passes the CAPA test suite.
2. Admin / auditor / manager smoke tests pass.
3. All custom tabs render safely under every role.
4. Route access matches the pre-roadmap baseline.
5. No empty-sidebar or ErrorBoundary reports for ≥ 2 release cycles.

## Pre-prompt validation
Before accepting the next Menu Setting roadmap phase, re-verify the four
invariants above. If any fails, pause the roadmap and patch CAPA first.

